Trace the resolution command-received stage for host-gap measurement.

The existing KORRI_RESW_TRACE instrumentation in src/video/v4l2m2m.c only sees a
resolution switch once new-size frames arrive from the host (size-change-detected
onward). That leaves the host encoder-reconfiguration gap -- the interval between
requesting a resolution change and the host emitting the first new-size frame --
invisible. Device measurements show the visible client-side pipeline is only
~50-100ms (dominated by the ~30ms decoder reopen, which patch 0010 made
load-bearing for frame correctness on the iris v4l2m2m path), yet the perceived
freeze can be larger, so the host gap must be quantified before deciding whether
any client-side work can make the switch seamless.

Add a self-contained command-received stamp in the local-control dispatcher,
emitted the instant a runtime.setResolution request is handed to the host
(before LiSendSunshineRuntimeSettingsMvp). It shares the same CLOCK_MONOTONIC
microsecond timeline as the decoder-side stamps, so command-received ->
size-change-detected measures the host gap directly. No-op unless
KORRI_RESW_TRACE is set, so it is safe to ship enabled.

diff --git a/src/local_control.c b/src/local_control.c
index 0f04ca0..9cb4d24 100644
--- a/src/local_control.c
+++ b/src/local_control.c
@@ -918,6 +918,28 @@ static struct json_object* moonlight_local_control_runtime_command_event(uint64_
   return event;
 }
 
+/* Korri resolution-switch timing trace -- host-gap measurement leg. Mirrors the
+ * sparse KORRI_RESW_TRACE appender in video/v4l2m2m.c (same CLOCK_MONOTONIC
+ * microsecond timeline) so the command-received stamp emitted here and the
+ * decoder-side stamps there share one clock: command-received ->
+ * size-change-detected measures the host encoder-reconfiguration gap that the
+ * decoder-side trace cannot see. No-op unless KORRI_RESW_TRACE is set, so it is
+ * safe to ship enabled. */
+static void korri_resw_trace_command(const char* stage) {
+  const char* path = getenv("KORRI_RESW_TRACE");
+  if (!path || !*path)
+    return;
+  struct timespec ts;
+  clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC, &ts);
+  unsigned long long now = (unsigned long long) ts.tv_sec * 1000000ULL
+                         + (unsigned long long) ts.tv_nsec / 1000ULL;
+  FILE* f = fopen(path, "a");
+  if (!f)
+    return;
+  fprintf(f, "%llu %s\n", now, stage);
+  fclose(f);
+}
+
 static int moonlight_local_control_dispatch_runtime_command(struct json_object* id, struct json_object* request, const char* method_name, int client_fd) {
   struct json_object* params = NULL;
   json_object_object_get_ex(request, "params", &params);
@@ -1004,6 +1026,11 @@ static int moonlight_local_control_dispatch_runtime_command(struct json_object*
   }
 
   uint32_t command_id = moonlight_local_control_next_command_id();
+  /* Stamp the instant we hand the resolution request to the host, before the
+   * wire send. Paired with the decoder-side size-change-detected stamp, the
+   * delta is the host encoder-reconfiguration gap. */
+  if (operation == MOONLIGHT_LC_OPERATION_SET_RESOLUTION)
+    korri_resw_trace_command("command-received");
   int send_result = LiSendSunshineRuntimeSettingsMvp(command_id, operation, value, secondary_value);
